            <ArticleTitle>Linkage and allelic association of chromosome 5 cytokine cluster genetic markers with atopy and asthma associated traits.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>15-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Linkage and association of polymorphic markers in the chromosome 5q31-q33 cytokine cluster to atopy and asthma associated phenotypes have been reported by a number of groups. To investigate this region, 29 polymorphic markers were used to genotype a combined set of 233 families. These markers were ordered based upon the genetic data, supplemented by published genetic and physical maps. Significant two-point linkage was observed for asthma (most significant marker IRF1, P = 0.0002) and atopy (CD14SNP, P = 0.0001). Allelic association was observed between D5S463 and atopy (P = 0.002) and the skin prick test index (P = 0.04). The data support the possibility of three asthma/atopy loci in the 5q31-q33 region, each with a relatively small effect.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright 2001 Academic Press.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
